{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>Which the prophet shall speak.</b> And he says: this thing will come upon you, and you see that it does not come — <b>that is the thing that YHWH did not speak.</b> And you kill him. And if you would say: this applies to one who prophesies about the future — what if he comes and says, 'Do such-and-such, and from the mouth of the Holy One, blessed be He, I say it'? You have already been commanded that if he comes to seduce you from any of the commandments, you shall not listen to him (Deuteronomy 13) — unless he is established for you as completely righteous, such as Elijah on Mount Carmel, who offered on a bamah at a time when bamot were forbidden, in order to build a fence for Israel — all according to the need of the hour and as a barricade against the breach. Therefore it is stated (verse 15), 'unto him you shall listen' (Sanhedrin 90)." "<b>You shall not be afraid of him.</b> You shall not withhold yourself from declaring him liable (Sifrei), and you shall not fear to punish him."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:47:39.594932674Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}